---
source: crates/rumps-query/tests/scripts.rs
description: "; Test: KILL statement\n; Tests deletion of variables and subtrees\n\n; Set up test data\nSET data(1) = \"one\"\nSET data(2) = \"two\"\nSET data(3) = \"three\"\nSET data(1, \"a\") = \"nested a\"\nSET data(1, \"b\") = \"nested b\"\n\n; Verify data exists\nLET v1 = GET data(1)\nOUTPUT v1\n; Expected: one\n\n; KILL single node\nKILL data(2)\n\n; Verify deleted\nLET v2 = GET data(2)\nOUTPUT v2\n; Expected: Option.None\n\n; KILL subtree\nKILL data(1)\n\n; Verify subtree deleted\nLET v3 = GET data(1)\nOUTPUT v3\n; Expected: Option.None\n\nLET v4 = GET data(1, \"a\")\nOUTPUT v4\n; Expected: Option.None\n\n; data(3) should still exist\nLET v5 = GET data(3)\nOUTPUT v5\n; Expected: three\n\n; KILL entire variable\nSET temp = 999\nLET before = GET temp\nOUTPUT before\n; Expected: 999\n\nKILL temp\nLET after = GET temp\nOUTPUT after\n; Expected: Option.None\n\n; KILL globals (in transaction)\nTRANSACTION {\n  SET ^TEST(1) = \"value1\"\n  SET ^TEST(2) = \"value2\"\n\n  KILL ^TEST(1)\n\n  LET g1 = GET ^TEST(1)\n  OUTPUT g1\n  ; Expected: Option.None\n\n  LET g2 = GET ^TEST(2)\n  OUTPUT g2\n  ; Expected: value2\n}\n\nOUTPUT \"KILL test complete\"\n"
---
